# cmd.exe parses batch files line by line and mishandles LF-only files around labels and
# parenthesised blocks. raw.githubusercontent.com serves the stored blob verbatim, so the
# CRLF has to be in the blob itself -- `text eol=crlf` would store LF and only convert on
# checkout, which does nothing for anyone curl-ing the raw URL.
*.cmd -text

*.sh  text eol=lf
*.ps1 text eol=lf
